1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,878
Chapter 72.

2
00:00:03,879 --> 00:00:06,435
The monkey rope.

3
00:00:06,436 --> 00:00:12,039
In the tumultuous business of cutting in and attending to a whale, there is much

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:17,318
running backwards and forwards among the crew. Now hands are wanted here, and

5
00:00:17,319 --> 00:00:22,999
then again hands are wanted there. There is no staying in any one place, for at

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,198
one in the same time everything has to be done everywhere. It is much the same

7
00:00:28,199 --> 00:00:33,079
with him who endeavors the description of the scene. We must now retrace our

8
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:38,039
way a little. It was mentioned that upon first breaking ground in the whale's

9
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,914
back, the blubber hook was inserted into the original hole there cut by the

10
00:00:42,915 --> 00:00:48,115
spades of the mates. But how did so clumsy and weighty a mass as that same

11
00:00:48,116 --> 00:00:53,558
hook get fixed in that hole? It was inserted there by my particular friend

12
00:00:53,559 --> 00:00:59,558
Quiqu whose duty it was as harpooner to descend upon the monster's back for the

13
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:05,719
special purpose referred to. But in very many cases circumstances require that

14
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:10,274
the harpooner shall remain on the whale till the whole tensing or stripping

15
00:01:10,275 --> 00:01:16,594
operation is concluded. The whale be it observed lies almost entirely submerged

16
00:01:16,595 --> 00:01:22,914
excepting the immediate parts operated upon. So down there, some 10 ft below

17
00:01:22,915 --> 00:01:27,399
the level of the deck, the poor harpooner flounders about, half on the

18
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:32,755
whale and half in the water, as the vast mass revolves like a treadmill beneath

19
00:01:32,756 --> 00:01:38,755
him. On the occasion in question, Quiqu figured in the Highland costume, a shirt

20
00:01:38,756 --> 00:01:43,479
and socks, in which, to my eyes at least, he appeared to uncommon

21
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:50,435
advantage, and no one had a better chance to observe him, as will presently be seen.

22
00:01:50,436 --> 00:01:55,719
Being the savage's bowsman, that is the person who pulled the bow ore in his

23
00:01:55,720 --> 00:02:00,679
boat, the second one from forward, it was my cheerful duty to attend upon him

24
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:05,799
while taking that hard scrabble scramble upon the dead whale's back. You have

25
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:11,719
seen Italian organ boys holding a dancing ape by a long cord. Just so from

26
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:16,838
the ship's steep side did I hold Quiquake down there in the sea by what

27
00:02:16,839 --> 00:02:21,954
is technically called in the fishery a monkey rope attached to a strong strip

28
00:02:21,955 --> 00:02:27,799
of canvas belted round his waist. It was a humorously perilous business for both

29
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:32,914
of us. For before we proceed further, it must be said that the monkey rope was

30
00:02:32,915 --> 00:02:38,999
fast at both ends, fast to Que's broad canvas belt and fast to my narrow

31
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:45,399
leather one. So that for better or for worse we too for the time were wedded.

32
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:50,838
And should poor Quiquake sink to rise no more, then both usage and honor demanded

33
00:02:50,839 --> 00:02:56,115
that instead of cutting the cord it should drag me down in his wake. So then

34
00:02:56,116 --> 00:02:59,719
an elongated Siamese ligature united us.

35
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:05,079
Quiqu was my own inseparable twin brother. Nor could I any way get rid of

36
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:10,679
the dangerous liabilities which the hemp and bond entailed.

37
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:15,954
So strongly and metaphysically did I conceive of my situation then that while

38
00:03:15,955 --> 00:03:20,838
earnestly watching his motions, I seemed distinctly to perceive that my own

39
00:03:20,839 --> 00:03:26,914
individuality was now merged in a joint stock company of two, that my free will

40
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:31,799
had received a mortal wound, and that another's mistake or misfortune might

41
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:37,558
plunge innocent me into unmmerited disaster and death. Therefore, I saw

42
00:03:37,559 --> 00:03:42,594
that here was a sort of interregnum in providence, for its even-handed equity

43
00:03:42,595 --> 00:03:46,039
never could have so gross an injustice.

44
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:50,518
And yet, still further pondering, while I jerked him now and then from between

45
00:03:50,519 --> 00:03:54,838
the whale and the ship, which would threaten to jam him, still further

46
00:03:54,839 --> 00:03:59,799
pondering, I say, I saw that this situation of mind was the precise

47
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:02,679
situation of every mortal that breathes.

48
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:07,638
only in most cases he one way or other has this Siamese connection with a

49
00:04:07,639 --> 00:04:12,755
plurality of other mortals. If your banker breaks, you snap. If your

50
00:04:12,756 --> 00:04:18,838
apothecary by mistake sends you poison in your pills, you die. True, you may

51
00:04:18,839 --> 00:04:24,039
say that by exceeding caution, you may possibly escape these and multitudinous

52
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:30,115
other evil chances of life. But handle Que's monkey rope heedfully as I would.

53
00:04:30,116 --> 00:04:35,558
Sometimes he jerked it so that I came very near sliding overboard. Nor could I

54
00:04:35,559 --> 00:04:40,838
possibly forget that do what I would, I had only the management of one end of

55
00:04:40,839 --> 00:04:47,079
it. Footnote. The monkey rope is found in all whalers, but it was only in the

56
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:51,799
peekquad that the monkey and his holder were ever tied together. This

57
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:57,238
improvement upon the original usage was introduced by no less a man than stub in

58
00:04:57,239 --> 00:05:01,878
order to afford the imperiled harpineer the strongest possible guarantee for the

59
00:05:01,879 --> 00:05:08,198
faithfulness and vigilance of his monkey rope holder. End a footnote.

60
00:05:08,199 --> 00:05:12,518
I have hinted that I would often jerk poor Quiquake from between the whale and

61
00:05:12,519 --> 00:05:16,838
the ship, where he would occasionally fall from the incessant rolling and

62
00:05:16,839 --> 00:05:22,838
swaying of both. But this was not the only jamming jeopardy he was exposed to.

63
00:05:22,839 --> 00:05:27,558
Unappalled by the massacre made upon them during the night, the sharks, now

64
00:05:27,559 --> 00:05:32,435
freshly and more keenly allured by the before pent blood which began to flow

65
00:05:32,436 --> 00:05:37,954
from the carcass, the rabid creatures swarmed round it like bees in a beehive.

66
00:05:37,955 --> 00:05:42,838
And right in among those sharks was Queiqu, who often pushed them aside with

67
00:05:42,839 --> 00:05:47,954
his floundering feet, a thing altogether incredible, were it not that attracted

68
00:05:47,955 --> 00:05:52,359
by such prey as a dead whale, the otherwise miscellaneous carnivorous

69
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:55,954
sharks will seldom touch a man.

70
00:05:55,955 --> 00:06:00,755
Nevertheless, it may well be believed that since they have such a ravenous

71
00:06:00,756 --> 00:06:06,115
finger in the pie, it is deemed but wise to look sharp to them. Accordingly,

72
00:06:06,116 --> 00:06:10,115
besides the monkey rope, with which I now and then jerked the poor fellow from

73
00:06:10,116 --> 00:06:15,954
too close of vicinity to the maw of what seemed a peculiarly ferocious shark, he

74
00:06:15,955 --> 00:06:20,198
was provided with still another protection. Suspended over the side in

75
00:06:20,199 --> 00:06:25,719
one of the stages, Tashego and Dagu continually flourished over his head a

76
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:30,198
couple of keen whale spades, wherewith they slaughtered as many sharks as they

77
00:06:30,199 --> 00:06:34,914
could reach. This procedure of theirs, to be sure, was very disinterested and

78
00:06:34,915 --> 00:06:39,719
benevolent of them. They meant Quiquake's best happiness, I admit, but

79
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:44,115
in their hasty zeal to befriend him, and from the circumstance that both he and

80
00:06:44,116 --> 00:06:48,999
the sharks were at times half hidden by the blood muddled water, those

81
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:54,359
indiscrete spades of theirs would come nearer amputating a leg than a tail. But

82
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:59,799
poor Quiquake, I suppose, straining and gasping there with that great iron hook.

83
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:04,999
Poor Quiquake, I suppose, only prayed to his yojo, and gave up his life into the

84
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,719
hands of his gods.

85
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:12,594
"Well, well, my dear comrade and twin brother," thought I, as I drew in, and

86
00:07:12,595 --> 00:07:17,878
then slacked off the rope to every swell of the sea. What matters it, after all?

87
00:07:17,879 --> 00:07:21,954
Are you not the precious image of each and all of us men in this whailing

88
00:07:21,955 --> 00:07:27,954
world? That unsounded ocean you gasp in is life. Those sharks your foes, those

89
00:07:27,955 --> 00:07:32,914
spades your friends. And what between sharks and spades you are in a sad

90
00:07:32,915 --> 00:07:38,359
pickle in peril, poor lad. But courage, there is good cheer in store for you,

91
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:44,039
Quiquake. For now, as with blue lips and bloodshot eyes, the exhausted savage at

92
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:48,755
last climbs up the chains, and stands all dripping and involuntarily trembling

93
00:07:48,756 --> 00:07:53,799
over the side, the steward advances, and with a benevolent, consolatory glance,

94
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:58,039
hands him what? Some hot cognac? No.

95
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:04,039
Hands him, ye God, hands him a cup of tepid ginger and water.

96
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:11,878
Ginger? Do I smell ginger? suspiciously asked stub coming near. "Yes, this must

97
00:08:11,879 --> 00:08:17,799
be ginger." Peering into the as yet untasted cup, then standing as if

98
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:22,274
incredulous for a while, he calmly walked toward the astonished steward,

99
00:08:22,275 --> 00:08:28,435
slowly saying, "Ginger, ginger. And will you have the goodness to tell me, Mr.

100
00:08:28,436 --> 00:08:34,359
Doughboy, where lies the virtue of ginger? Ginger? Is ginger the sort of

101
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:40,999
fuel you use, doughboy, to kindle a fire in this shivering cannibal? Ginger? What

102
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:49,079
the devil is ginger? Sea coal, firewood, Lucifer matches, tinder, gunpowder. What

103
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:56,039
the devil is ginger? I say that you offer this cup to our poor Quag here.

104
00:08:56,040 --> 00:09:00,518
There is some sneaking temperance society movement about this business, he

105
00:09:00,519 --> 00:09:04,518
suddenly added, now approaching Starbucks, who had just come from

106
00:09:04,519 --> 00:09:07,399
forward. Will you look at that, sir?

107
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:11,479
Smell of it if you please. Then, watching the mate's countenance, he

108
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:17,399
added, "The steward, Mr. Starbucks, had the face to offer that calam and jallop

109
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:22,755
to Quiquake there this instant off the whale. Is the steward an apothecary,

110
00:09:22,756 --> 00:09:27,479
sir? And may I ask whether this is the sort of bitters by which he blows back

111
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:30,914
the life into a half-drowned man.

112
00:09:30,915 --> 00:09:38,755
I trust not, said Starbucks. It is poor stuff enough. I I steward cried Stub.

113
00:09:38,756 --> 00:09:40,914
We'll teach you to drug it, Harpaneer.

114
00:09:40,915 --> 00:09:43,719
None of your apothecaries medicine here.

115
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:48,594
You want to poison us, do you? You have got out insurance on our lives and want

116
00:09:48,595 --> 00:09:52,435
to murder us all and pocket the proceeds, do you?

117
00:09:52,436 --> 00:09:57,479
It was not me, cried Doughboy. It was Aunt Charity that brought the ginger on

118
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:02,039
board, and Badme never give the harpooners any spirits, but only this

119
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:08,838
ginger jub, so she called it. Ginger Job, you gingery rascal. Take that and

120
00:10:08,839 --> 00:10:13,399
run along with you to the lockers and get something better. I hope I do no

121
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:17,878
wrong, Mr. Starbucks. It is the captain's orders. Grog for the harpooner

122
00:10:17,879 --> 00:10:21,399
on a whale. Enough, replied Starbucks.

123
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:26,518
only don't hit him again. But oh, I never hurt when I hit except when I hit

124
00:10:26,519 --> 00:10:31,479
a whale or something of that sort, and this fellow's a weasel. What were you

125
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:38,518
about saying, sir? Only this. Go down with him, and get what thou wantest thyself.

126
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:43,719
When Stub reappeared, he came with a dark flask in one hand, and a sort of

127
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:48,115
tea caddy in the other. The first contained strong spirits, and was handed

128
00:10:48,116 --> 00:10:56,800
to Quiqu. The second was Aunt Charity's gift, and that was freely given to the waves.
